From: DIR-842 R1 port
Subject: [PATCH] gpio: realtek-otto: add the RTL819x (RTL8197F) variant

Same controller block as the switch SoCs, but these router parts are
little-endian, so the registers are accessed in native port order -- the same
layout the driver already calls "reversed". Line interrupts are not wired on
these boards, so declare them unavailable rather than registering an irqchip
that can never fire.

--- a/drivers/gpio/gpio-realtek-otto.c	2026-09-02 13:27:21.149243274 -0300
+++ b/drivers/gpio/gpio-realtek-otto.c	2026-09-02 13:27:21.157243558 -0300
@@ -345,6 +345,15 @@
 		.compatible = "realtek,rtl8390-gpio",
 	},
 	{
+		/*
+		 * RTL819x router SoCs: same register block, native (non
+		 * byte-swapped) port order because the CPU is little-endian.
+		 * Line interrupts are not wired up on these boards.
+		 */
+		.compatible = "realtek,rtl8197f-gpio",
+		.data = (void *)(GPIO_PORTS_REVERSED | GPIO_INTERRUPTS_DISABLED)
+	},
+	{
 		.compatible = "realtek,rtl9300-gpio",
 		.data = (void *)(GPIO_PORTS_REVERSED | GPIO_INTERRUPTS_PER_CPU)
 	},
